==English==

===Etymology===
{{m|en|LOL}} (Initialism of laughing out loud.) + {{m|en|-z}} (Eye dialect spelling variant of the plural suffix {{m|en|-s}}.)

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|Internet slang|leet}} {{alternative form of|en|LOL}}

====Usage notes====
The final {{m|en||Z}} serves only to make the acronym look like a plural noun, or, more commonly, as a mockery of those who use {{m|en|-z|z}} to pluralize other nouns, as opposed to {{m|en|-s|s}}. The mockery of such people is often not done in any kind of specific context, but usually as a way to lighten up a conversation.

